(Bug #27 regression: a Repeat that is not the last action in an If
 branch. The Repeat owns its trailing period (rule 1), which then serves
 as the separator, so the next action `Print "b"` follows with no comma
 and belongs to the If's then-block — exactly as a nested While or For
 each already behaves. Because the If condition is false, neither "a"
 nor "b" runs; only "after", at the top level, prints. Before the fix the
 Repeat absorbed "b" and "after" into its body, but the false condition
 swallowed the whole branch, so nothing printed at all. Expected:
 after.)

If false then,
    Repeat 2 times, Print "a".
    Print "b".
Print "after".